pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Regression test (wrong verdict): the same defect as
% proof_by_contradiction_proofgoal_not_contradiction, aimed at a SATISFIABLE
% formula instead of a tautology. `x1 = 1, x2 = 0` satisfies both constraints
% -- see the companion proof_by_contradiction_fabricated_proofgoal under
% correct/version3, which certifies exactly that -- yet this used to verify as
% `s VERIFIED UNSATISFIABLE`.
%
% `proofgoal 1` inside the `pbc` was answered with a goal invented from
% database constraint 1, whose discharge is free, and discharging it set
% `contradiction_proven`, so the `pbc` added `+1 ~x1 >= 1` without ever showing
% a contradiction from `1 x1 >= 1`. With `~x1` in the database the following
% `rup >= 1` then closed the proof.
f 2;
pbc +1 ~x1 >= 1 : subproof
    proofgoal 1
        pol -1 1 +;
    qed;
qed;
rup >= 1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : -1;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
